  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a **permutation** P=[P1,P2,…,PN]P = [P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_N]P=[P1​,P2​,…,PN​] of {1,2,3,…,N}\\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,3,…,N}.\n\nCount the number of pairs (i,j)(i,j)(i,j) such that:\n\n\n1≤i≤j≤N1 \\leq i \\leq j \\leq N1≤i≤j≤N\ni+ji+ji+j divides Pi+PjP_i+P_jPi​+Pj​.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the length of PPP.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated distinct integers P1,P2,P3,…,PNP_1, P_2, P_3, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,P3​,…,PN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of pairs satisfying the given condition.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1061 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^61≤N≤2⋅106",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\leq P_i \\leq N1≤Pi​≤N for each 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.",
      "All elements of PPP are **distinct**.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1062 \\cdot 10^62⋅106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
